# HVST-bz-10 section 2 -- THE STOP, by the runner's OWN stop file. NOTHING WAS KILLED.
# by 0.7.0_AE_CloudOps~ZW on site Z, written 2026-10-13T23:57:25Z

## (i) the stop-file path, READ from the task's own --stop-file argument, never typed from memory
C:\Users\Opal Bloomberg\Desktop\wk-harvest-runner-pin-995adcaeaa\.runtime\harvest-cycle\STOP
created at 2026-10-13T23:51:41Z (CreationTimeUtc read off the file itself, 0 bytes)
DEVIATION, RECORDED: its PARENT DIRECTORY did not exist. '.runtime' was present under the old pin but
'.runtime\harvest-cycle' was not, so a plain New-Item FAILED (DirectoryNotFoundException) and I created the
directory first. The runner polls the path with Path(stop_file).exists() (cycle_runner.py:297 at the RUNNING
pin), so an existence poll is all it needs -- but until this act the baked stop-file path named a directory
that was never created, i.e. the graceful-stop mechanism had no place to put its file. Row filed.

